// The Bernoulli Effect: Unveiling the Inverse Relationship Between Fluid Speed and Pressure: A direct and critical consequence of energy conservation mandates an inverse relationship between the fluid's kinetic energy (speed) and its static pressure component. Consequently, in regions where the fluid streamlines are constricted, causing the flow speed ($v$) to accelerate, the corresponding static pressure ($P$) must necessarily decrease to maintain the constant energy sum.
